<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muzaffar Jung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1751</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muzaffar Jung was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-jah-i">Asaf Jah I</a> who claimed the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> after 1748 with French support. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanda-sahib">Chanda Sahib</a>, he won at Ambur in 1749, and after his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-jung">Nasir Jung</a>'s death in December 1750 he became Nizam. He was killed only weeks later, in February 1751, by rebellious Pathan nawabs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muzaffar-jung.jpg" alt="Muzaffar Jung" width="195" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muzaffar_Jung.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
